WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:04.740
Yeah, you can still remember your teammates and you tend to call them or keep up with them.

2
00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:08.940
I guess because you live with them, you . . . You’re in the dormitory with them.

3
00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:09.620
We were.

4
00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:13.500
I don’t know if they going to still continue this, but . . . We ate together.

5
00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.720
We went to class together, a lot of times.

6
00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:21.060
We practiced with each other two and three hours a day.

7
00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:23.000
We were just around each other a lot.

8
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.860
And we knew that the four years that we were going to be there,

9
00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:31.100
or the two years, or whatever, that they were going to be there next year.

10
00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:39.820
In the NFL there’s a different story because you tend not to want to get too close to someone because you don’t know if they’re going to be there six weeks from now.

11
00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:47.020
You don’t know if they’re going to be there two years from now or one year because of the high turnover that they have in the NFL.

12
00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:54.500
You know the average career when I was playing was only four years, at most.

13
00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:56.360
I don’t know what it is now.

14
00:00:56.360 --> 00:01:04.200
So, you really don’t get to know these guys and you don’t . . . You’re not with them as much because,

15
00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.400
the off season, most guys go to their homes.

16
00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:07.700
I know I used to come back to Louisiana.

17
00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:11.640
Once the season was over I was gone, I’d come down South.

18
00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:16.520
Only for the football season though, those were the only times that you’re really with those guys.

19
00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:22.840
So I guess that’s why you tend not to become as close to those guys as you would in college.
